        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> > > This module doesn't open map by default and [doesn't create mappings for it](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ab94192dd36b35c6752aac7154c7130922c27af7/doc/mini-map.txt#L143).\r\n> > > Does executing `:lua MiniMap.open()` solves the issue?\r\n> > \r\n> > \r\n> > Ahhhh.. Yes, it does. Thank you. I will figure a way to open this by default then. Thank you!\r\n> \r\n> With reasonably structured config you can probably add `MiniMap.open()` line just after `require('mini.map').setup()`.\r\n\r\nYes, that works.. The issue now is that, since I am using nvim-tree and I like Nvim-tree to automatically close when I close the last buffer.. that no longer works with the mini-map opened. Any suggestion or recipe for this case? Have mini-map close when I close the file?",
