        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Yes, that works.. The issue now is that, since I am using nvim-tree and I like Nvim-tree to automatically close when I close the last buffer.. that no longer works with the mini-map opened. Any suggestion or recipe for this case? Have mini-map close when I close the file?\r\n\r\nI don't quite remember how this is implemented in 'nvim-tree' (or maybe you are using the custom solution). 'mini.map' creates a scratch buffer which I'd argue shouldn't be taken into account when implementing \"close when no buffer left\" functionality. I'd suggest either update logic of when 'nvim-tree' is closed or close map as a substitute of \"close the last buffer\".",
